  "facts": [
    "The Cross Bay Veterans Memorial Bridge, originally opened in 1925, was rebuilt into a low‑level bascule bridge in 1939, costing $33 million—about $388 million today—to ease congestion that plagued the original 1925 structure.",
    "In 1970, the current high‑level fixed bridge rose 55 feet, allowing boats to pass beneath without delays, a design choice that eliminated the previous drawbridge’s traffic bottlenecks and modernized Jamaica Bay’s infrastructure.",
    "Starting February 2024, Queens residents with NYCSC E‑ZPass receive a 100 % toll rebate on the Cross Bay Bridge, a policy that rewards local commuters and reflects recent MTA budget adjustments."
  ],
